 learning, art/3D/creative. Reads the request four ways (literal, inverse, adjacent, reframed), verifies the real facts instead of guessing from memory (grep the codebase, read the actual documents and numbers, search official sources), checks a 12-axis impact surface (existing state, conflicts, limits and deadlines, security/legal, partial failure, backward compatibility, scale, recurring cost, observability, edge cases, checks, reversibility), runs a domain-specific premortem, then delivers at most 5 ranked risks with exact proof and a concrete verification each, ending in a GO / NO-GO verdict at paid-specialist precision, never generic. Use whenever the user says \"pense à tout\", \"think of everything\", \"qu'est-ce que j'ai oublié\", \"what am I missing\", asks what a change or decision might break, or wants a premortem, dependency check, or impact analysis. Also trigger proactively, without the phrase, before shipping anything touching shared state, storage or quotas, concurrency, auth or permissions, payments, a public API/route — or any decision that is expensive, irreversible, or deadline-bound.\n- translate-srt-selectlanguage: Traduit les sous-titres d'un ou plusieurs mkv (ou .srt direct) vers une langue cible (défaut FR depuis l'anglais) puis remuxe la piste traduite dans le mkv sans réencodage. Sélection de langue source/cible parmi les pistes détectées ; STOP immédiat si la langue cible existe déjà dans le fichier. Détecte les fichiers corrompus/téléchargements incomplets avant de travailler. Utiliser quand Matthieu demande de traduire des sous-titres, ajouter un SRT français à des épisodes, ou \"translate puis remux\". Inclut aussi l'ancien mode /translate : traducteur CLI concis FR/EN/JP mot ou phrase.\n- ytb-dlp: <!-- MANPAGE: BEGIN EXCLUDED SECTION -->\n- zenray-backup-mirror: Déclencher, monitorer ou arrêter le second système de backup ZenRayProgress (scripts/backup-mirror.mjs — miroir froid indépendant, second exemplaire des binaires ZenRayShards sur des repos privés séparés). Déclencheurs — \"lance le backup\", \"vérifie le second backup\", \"sauvegarde en double tel dossier\", \"où en est le backup-mirror\", \"monitore le backup\". JAMAIS lancer le run complet sans confirmation explicite de Matthieu — toujours proposer --dry-run --limit=N en premier.\n- zenrayprogress-context: Load the current ZenRayProgress implementation context directly from its local repository. Use before implementing, debugging, reviewing, or operating ZenRayProgress instead of manually selecting project files.\n- zenrayshards-upload-media: Skill UNIQUE d'upload média ZenRayProgress — route fichiers locaux vidéo/image/audio et liens YouTube vers ZenRayShards v2. Vidéo privée chiffrée+hvc1 ; image publique jsDelivr ; audio public jsDelivr mais chiffré AES-GCM en parts dont le ciphertext ne dépasse jamais 19 MiB. Intègre aussi toutes les règles Git bulk : dès 100 fichiers ou pour toute réparation/migration/réindexation, inventaire local puis clone/pull/commit/push Git, jamais REST/raw dans une boucle. Déclencheurs — upload ZenRayShards, upload vidéo/image/audio/musique, chemin local ou lien youtube.com/youtu.be destiné à Create. Si le dossier cible manque, DEMANDER, jamais deviner.\n- zenrayshelf-create-card: Create one or a few ZenRayProgress Shelf cards from Codex or Claude with an automatically ingested poster. Use for Games, Anime & Manga, Movies, Series & Docs, or Books; default to In Progress and N/A score when omitted.\n- deep-research: Deep research harness — fan-out web searches, fetch sources, adversarially verify claims, synthesize a cited report. - When the user wants a deep, multi-source, fact-checked research report on any topic. BEFORE invoking, check if the question is specific enough to research directly — if underspecified (e.g., \"what car to buy\" without budget/use-case/region), ask 2-3 clarifying questions to narrow scope. Then pass the refined question as args, weaving the answers in.\n- anthropic-skills:consolidate-memory: Reflective pass over your memory files — merge duplicates, fix stale facts, prune the index.\n- anthropic-skills:docx: Use this skill whenever the user wants to create, read, edit, or manipulate Word documents (.docx files) or Word templates (.dotx files). Triggers include: any mention of 'Word doc', 'word document', '.docx', '.dotx', or requests to produce professional documents with formatting like tables of contents, headings, page numbers, or letterheads. Also use when extracting or reorganizing content from .docx or .dotx files, inserting or replacing images in documents, performing find-and-replace in Word files, working with tracked changes or comments, or converting content into a polished Word document. If the user asks for a 'report', 'memo', 'letter', 'template', or similar deliverable as a Word or .docx file, use this skill. Do NOT use for PDFs, spreadsheets, Google Docs, or general coding tasks unrelated to document generation.\n- anthropic-skills:kanji-stroke-order: Generate a textbook-style stroke-order diagram (SVG) for any Japanese character (kanji, hiragana, or katakana). Produces one panel per stroke showing completed strokes in black, the current stroke highlighted with a red number and directional arrow at its starting point, and remaining strokes ghosted in light gray. Use this skill whenever the user asks how to write a Japanese character, requests stroke order, asks \"in what order do I draw X\", wants to learn or memorize a kanji, asks to decompose a character into strokes, says \"show me the strokes for X\", mentions 書き順 / kakijun, or shows a stroke-order chart and asks for one for a different character. Trigger even when the user only provides a single character and the intent is implicit from the language-learning context.\n- anthropic-skills:mcp-builder: Guide for creating high-quality MCP (Model Context Protocol) servers that enable LLMs to interact with external services through well-designed tools. Use when building MCP servers to integrate external APIs or services, whether in Python (FastMCP) or Node/TypeScript (MCP SDK).\n- anthropic-skills:pdf: Use this skill whenever the user wants to do anything with PDF files. This includes reading or extracting text/tables from PDFs, combining or merging multiple PDFs into one, splitting PDFs apart, rotating pages, adding watermarks, creating new PDFs, filling PDF forms, encrypting/decrypting PDFs, extracting images, and OCR on scanned PDFs to make them searchable. If the user mentions a .pdf file or asks to produce one, use this skill.\n- anthropic-skills:pptx: Use this skill any time a .pptx or .potx file is involved in any way — as input, output, or both. This includes: creating slide decks, pitch decks, or presentations; reading, parsing, or extracting text from any .pptx or .potx file (even if the extracted content will be used elsewhere, like in an email or summary); editing, modifying, or updating existing presentations; combining or splitting slide files; working with templates (.potx), layouts, speaker notes, or comments. Trigger whenever the user mentions \"deck,\" \"slides,\" \"presentation,\" or references a .pptx or .potx filename, regardless of what they plan to do with the content afterward. If a .pptx or .potx file needs to be opened, created, or touched, use this skill.\n- anthropic-skills:schedule: Create or update a scheduled task that runs automatically. Use when the user says things like \"every day\", \"each morning\", \"remind me in an hour\", \"run this at noon\", or wants to reschedule an existing task.\n- anthropic-skills:setup-cowork: Guided Cowork setup — install role-matched plugins, connect your tools, try a skill.\n- anthropic-skills:skill-creator: Create new skills, modify and improve existing skills, and measure skill performance. Use when users want to create a skill from scratch, edit, or optimize an existing skill, run evals to test a skill, benchmark skill performance with variance analysis, or optimize a 